From 6709a1dfd330ff727fc3a52d25757124ad84d4f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:18:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Fix verification result presentation (false failures, 'user
 aborted request')

Backend: a provider response that does not prove failure - 'pending/processing'
status, 5xx/408 gateway errors, unreadable body (Hubbu) or a 45s timeout /
gateway error (K-Tech) - is now treated as outcome-unknown: the transaction
stays PENDING (no refund, no 'failed') and is flagged on
/admin/provider-reconciliation. Explicit rejections still fail and refund.

Web: slip pages waited only 20s while the provider can take ~45s+, so the
browser aborted ('The user aborted a request') while the server went on to
succeed. Slip calls now wait 110s, report a cut-off as 'still processing -
do not resubmit' instead of an error, send a per-input Idempotency-Key so a
retry replays rather than double-bills, and poll Recent requests so the
finished document appears by itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015YoLAo63RFk6PcWruuMD9h
